The '''2006 FIFA Club World Cup''' (officially known as the '''FIFA Club World Cup Japan 2006 presented by Toyota''' for sponsorship reasons) was a [[Association football|football]] tournament held in [[Japan]] between 10 and 17 December 2006. It was the third [[FIFA Club World Cup]].

The club champions from each of the six confederations played in a knockout tournament. The quarter-final match-ups were determined by a draw including the [[Asian Football Confederation|AFC]], [[Confederation of African Football|CAF]], [[CONCACAF]] and [[Oceania Football Confederation|OFC]] champions, while the [[UEFA]] and [[CONMEBOL]] champions were given byes to the semi-finals. The losers of the quarter-finals played for fifth place, while the losers of the semi-finals played in a third-place play-off.

Defending champions [[São Paulo FC|São Paulo]] were beaten in the [[2006 Copa Libertadores Finals]] by fellow Brazilian side [[Sport Club Internacional|Internacional]], who went on to win the Club World Cup for the first time, beating [[Al Ahly SC|Al Ahly]] in the semi-finals before defeating Spanish club [[FC Barcelona|Barcelona]] 1–0 in the [[2006 FIFA Club World Cup Final|final]].

A team from the host nation did not participate, as was initially proposed. Following the departure of [[Football Federation Australia|Australia]] from the OFC, the Oceanian representative, [[Auckland City FC|Auckland City]], was fully amateur, so forcing them to play a play-off for a place in the quarter-finals against the [[J. League Division 1|J. League]] champions ([[Gamba Osaka]]) was considered, which would have also promoted local interest. The change would have also eliminated the fifth-place play-off, to keep the number of games intact. This was finally rejected, but the tournament format was changed for [[2007 FIFA Club World Cup|2007]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://chinadaily.com.cn/sports/2006-06/05/content_608467.htm |title=Oceania to get direct entry to Club World Cup |access-date=12 July 2006 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120118090055/http://www.chinadaily.com.cn/sports/2006-06/05/content_608467.htm |archive-date=18 January 2012 |url-status=dead  }}</ref>

